xnu: run the M3 work after the log thread is up, and flush before the risky writes

gmu=2 reset the machine with nothing in the ring: the loader runs in
SweetAdreno::start(), which is before bsd_init, so the UFS log thread has not
started yet and nothing reaches the partition. Moving the work ten seconds later
puts it after the log thread begins flushing every 5 s, so even a full SoC reset
now leaves the last lines on disk.

  - sweetadreno_gmu / sweetadreno_smmu work is handed to a kernel thread that
    sleeps sweetadreno_delay seconds (default 10, capped at 120).
  - sweet_log_flush_now() is called immediately before the CX halt write and
    again before CM3_SYSRESET is released, so the expensive-to-reproduce lines
    are on disk before the two writes that previously killed the machine.
  - If the thread cannot be created the work still runs inline, with a log line
    saying so.

The host harness grew stubs for kernel_thread_start/IOSleep/sweet_log_flush_now
(同步执行、睡眠记账), so both paths stay testable without a device.
